group: D2h
formula: C2H4
construction: two equivalent halves
headline: 
note: Fragments: two equivalent halves · energies in Hartree · labels in D<sub>2h</sub> · 2 core orbitals hidden\nB3U: 2B3u has no partner among the levels drawn and is shown as non-bonding
about: **What is drawn.** The molecular levels in the middle are the calculation's own orbital energies, in Hartree.\n\n**Fragment levels.** Each fragment level is placed at the mean of the molecular orbitals it became, weighted by its share of them, and kept in the atom's own shell order. Its free-atom energy is given beside it.\n\n**Symmetry.** Symmetry labels computed from the orbitals in D2h; the code reported none.  b1 and b2 (b2 and b3 in D2h) depend on the choice of axes; ECCE follows Mulliken's convention, as most textbooks do.\n\n**Not shown.** 2 core orbitals below −10.17 Hartree.
